                        "entry_id": "24913f09-d426-31d8-8ad8-9bbee920a57e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The tendency to treat the Sabbath as a solemn religious occasion rather than merely as a day off."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dff43940-e653-41d4-9b05-6d474802257c",
                                "sense_id": "f9e2a8db-9b5f-33c2-a483-615232c96352",
                                "text": "[…] they do not want the lowest forms of excitement, or of literature; they want something which shall occupy the middle ground between the debauchery of low holidayism and the religious observance which comes with Sabbathism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e416ca3b-df27-49c2-8605-3a6090489c4b",
                                "sense_id": "f9e2a8db-9b5f-33c2-a483-615232c96352",
                                "text": "As to Sunday legislation we have seen that its origin was absolutely pagan, and that it has been destructive of true Sabbathism at all times."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
